  "releaseNotes": "Breaking:\n- switched Fourier transforms used for calculating unvoiced part to symmetric normalization (makes older .esp files incompatible)\n        \nNon-breaking:\n- tuned Kalman filter used for voiced part smoothing\n- switched pitch shifting to use zeros instead of unvoiced spectrum for extremely high frequencies\n- adjusted synthesis time unvoiced normalization to match Rayleigh distribution scale factor to mean ratio\n- made separation Kalman filter strength configurable\n- added Kalman filter post-smoothing at analysis time to unvoiced component",
